            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GoldWater4457"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My mom used to make these, and then my late husband and I made them as part of our annual Christmas boxes that we used to give to friends. I lost the recipe and haven't made them in years so I am glad I found this one. However, my recipe was not quite the same. We never added pecans or red sugar, and I don't remember using gelatin. To finish them off we dipped them in strawberry jello powder and I piped the leaves using green icing. They tasted great.",
            "datePublished": "2024-11-09T02:58:28.963Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jessica53214"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this recipe my grandmother had it in one of her old Utility Company cookbooks, we made them every year together. They always look so pretty!!\n\nUpdate! This year I used different flavored gelatins and just shaped them into small balls. They turned out fabulous!",
            "datePublished": "2008-01-14T11:56:50.877Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TACZYZ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this recipe. I have been making it for years. I found it in an old candy cookbook. They are definitely sweet, but it's candy, what do you expect. And make sure you use sweetened condensed milk not evaporated, because yes, there is a difference. Just a suggestion, in my recipe it says to use ground coconut too. I just put both the pecans and coconut together in the food processor and grind them both. This makes the berries form a little easier.",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-20T10:56:56.323Z"
          },
          {
