            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "dutchiev"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My cousin gave me this recipe years ago. I lost it when we moved and I am so glad I found it here in time for my daughter's baby shower next week. I love it. The only thing I do differently is I do most of the berry in red and the top on green therefore I do not have to make the almond paste.",
            "datePublished": "2014-02-11T12:40:30.810Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jessi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very fun recipe! I had left over green colored chocolate from Christmas candy and sliced off slivers to use for the strawberry tops. That worked well. I decorated a cake (lemon and strawberry marbled) with leaves and then placed candy strawberries on top for beautiful spring cake. Definitely allow plenty of time for chilling so the candy isn't too sticky to work with. I didn't have colored sugar so just rolled in white sugar to give a little sparkle. The strawberries were very popular!",
            "datePublished": "2008-03-25T07:36:46.467Z"
          },
          {
